Chapter: IntLiteralOverflow

 The literal below is the X25519 field prime, 2 to the 255 minus 19.
 It cannot fit in a 64-bit Integer; before CDX2071 the compiler
 silently truncated it to the low 64 bits, which is how the original
 DiffieHellman implementation shipped structurally broken.

Section: Definitions

  big-prime : Integer = 57896044618658097711785492504343953926634992332820282019728792003956564819949

  opening : Text = show big-prime

